{"parentUuid":"13a52a9b-44d8-43ed-a96c-f370912242ae","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014F1AMTJZveg7L2Pv2qnuD8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M6D8cjRQGMpBGBapgPZL6Y","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"2D packing placement LP relaxation strength gap integer programming cuts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8059,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":237,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8059},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8059,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosQSRNTtKnxz5sQeMMu","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dc3e33cb-4216-476d-843f-19682fe8aa50","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:27.877Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dc3e33cb-4216-476d-843f-19682fe8aa50","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6D8cjRQGMpBGBapgPZL6Y","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D packing placement LP relaxation strength gap integer programming cuts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"An introduction to the two‐dimensional rectangular cutting and packing problem - Oliveira - 2023 - International Transactions in Operational Research - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/itor.13236\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"Improved approximation algorithms for multidimensional bin packing problems | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4031404\"},{\"title\":\"Relaxations and Bounds: Applications to Knapsack Problems\",\"url\":\"https://sofdem.github.io/teach/oro/m2oro-ilp-demassey-notes-lec7-8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LP Relaxation and Tree Packing for Minimum $k$-Cut\",\"url\":\"https://chekuri.cs.illinois.edu/papers/kcut-revisited-sidma.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LP Relaxation and Tree Packing for Minimum $k$-cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/327110746_LP_Relaxation_and_Tree_Packing_for_Minimum_k-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"LP bounds in various constraint programming approaches for orthogonal packing - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0305054811003650\"},{\"title\":\"Exact solutions for the 2d-strip packing problem using the positions-and-covering methodology - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7808675/\"},{\"title\":\"LP Relaxation and Tree Packing for Minimum k-cuts - DROPS\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/OASIcs.SOSA.2019.7\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about 2D packing problems and LP relaxation approaches. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## LP Relaxation in 2D Packing Problems\n\nStrengthening linear programming (LP)-relaxations in 2D packing problems can be achieved through restrictions on item quantities, though this increases the difficulty of corresponding column generation problems.\n\n## Exact Methods and LP-Based Approaches\n\nThe Column Generation method addresses the exponential number of columns (variables) in linear programs by starting with a restricted model that only includes a subset of columns and iteratively adding columns that may improve the current solution.\n\nResearchers have adapted 1D relaxation bounds based on linear programming into constraint propagation processes for 2D orthogonal packing problems, investigating constraint programming approaches with dichotomy and disjunctive branching strategies.\n\n## LP Relaxations and Bounds\n\nDifferent types of bounds are used in 2D packing, including volume bounds, dual-feasible functions, conservative scales, and 1D bar relaxations. Conservative scales involve modified item sizes that preserve feasibility while providing valid inequalities for binary knapsack polyhedra.\n\n## Integer Programming with Cuts\n\nIn branch-and-cut approaches for 2D bin packing, cuts are added to exclude infeasible assignments of items to bins when subproblems are found to be infeasible.\n\nThe search results show active research in combining LP relaxations with constraint programming and integer programming cuts for solving 2D packing problems, though specific details about integrality gap measures would require more specialized literature on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e050b8e7-93e8-4305-82b1-4340bfe082cb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:35.077Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc3e33cb-4216-476d-843f-19682fe8aa50","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"13a52a9b-44d8-43ed-a96c-f370912242ae","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9ZaibNnhfqP7PSF6zUXrE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT linearization_level LP relaxation cuts add_clique_cuts add_zero_half_cuts add_mir_cuts add_rlt_cuts OR-Tools\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MIP aspects of OR-tools CP-SAT solver. Frederic Didier (fdid@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://www.mixedinteger.org/EUROMIP/2025/slides/frederic-didier.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"linear_relaxation | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/linear_relaxation\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www-eio.upc.es/lceio/manuals/cplex-11/html/usrcplex/solveMIP14.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT's linearization level and cutting planes in Google OR-Tools:\n\n## CP-SAT Linearization and LP Relaxation with Cutting Planes\n\nAt root level, even cutting planes such as Gomory-Cuts are applied to improve the linear relaxation. The linear relaxation is implemented as a propagator and potentially executed at every node in the search tree but only at lowest priority. A significant difference to the application of linear relaxations in branch and bound algorithms is that only some pivot iterations are performed (to make it faster).\n\n### Linearization Levels\n\nCP-SAT supports different linearization strategies: `default_lp` (LCG-based search with default linearization of the model), `max_lp` (same as default_lp but with maximal linearization), and `no_lp` (same as default_lp but without linearization).\n\n### Cutting Planes in OR-Tools\n\nCP-SAT's base LP only uses integer coefficients (scaled for the LP solver), and any cuts generated are also pure integer. Key actions involve adding cut generators and appending relaxations for various constraint types, including: `AllDiff`, `Circuit`, `Cumulative`, `IntProd`, `LinMax`, `NoOverlap`, and `Routes`.\n\nThe search results contain technical presentations and documentation about CP-SAT's implementation but do not provide detailed information specifically about the individual cut parameters you mentioned (`add_clique_cuts`, `add_zero_half_cuts`, `add_mir_cuts`, `add_rlt_cuts`). The documentation indicates that the zero-half cut function and MIR (Mixed Integer Rounding) cuts are implemented techniques in the solver, but detailed parameter documentation for these specific cut options was not found in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"598ac166-a33e-40c0-b6d1-e3c06fbb37c7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:35.577Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"13a52a9b-44d8-43ed-a96c-f370912242ae","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
