{"parentUuid":"9d8fdb23-8f21-47c3-b908-1deb8e71326b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_016okmDNeK2NockrC7XcA91J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XEwXWs6Q3kaaLpXmzA1dRY","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"hybrid CP MIP Lagrangian relaxation lower bound CP-SAT branch and bound cooperation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_read_input_tokens":21172,"output_tokens":323,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1728},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1408,"output_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":21172,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1728,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosRPF9i5s7CnVLgvMqy","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4fc24998-213d-48f6-bcfb-c9305b1c82c5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:41.016Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9d8fdb23-8f21-47c3-b908-1deb8e71326b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JFgcEXLSGhTufPoGwuWCMK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PDLP OR-Tools large scale LP first order primal dual hybrid gradient\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2106.04756] Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.04756\"},{\"title\":\"[2501.07018] PDLP: A Practical First-Order Method for Large-Scale Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.07018\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl: Experimental first-order solvers for linear and quadratic programming. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-research/FirstOrderLp.jl\"},{\"title\":\"PDLP: A Practical First-Order Method for Large-Scale Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.07018v1\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/8439.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practical large-scale linear programming using primal-dual hybrid gradient | Proceedings of the 35th International Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.5555/3540261.3541809\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://papers.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2021/file/a8fbbd3b11424ce032ba813493d95ad7-Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2021/hash/a8fbbd3b11424ce032ba813493d95ad7-Abstract.html\"},{\"title\":\"Scaling up linear programming with PDLP\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/blog/scaling-up-linear-programming-with-pdlp/\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=_eXwwWOyqT_\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about PDLP and its integration with OR-Tools. Here are the key findings:\n\n## PDLP Overview\n\nPDLP is a practical first-order method for linear programming (LP) that can solve to the high levels of accuracy that are expected in traditional LP applications. It can scale to very large problems because its core operation is matrix-vector multiplications.\n\n## Technical Foundation\n\nPDLP is derived by applying the primal-dual hybrid gradient (PDHG) method, popularized by Chambolle and Pock (2011), to a saddle-point formulation of LP.\n\n## Key Enhancements\n\nPDLP enhances PDHG for LP by combining several new techniques with older tricks from the literature; the enhancements include diagonal preconditioning, presolving, adaptive step sizes, and adaptive restarting.\n\n## OR-Tools Integration\n\nA C++ implementation of the PDLP algorithm is included in OR-Tools. Key new contributions include feasibility polishing, a technique that quickly finds solutions that are approximately optimal but almost exactly feasible, and a multithreaded C++ implementation available in Google OR-Tools.\n\n## Performance\n\nPDLP was compared with SCS, an ADMM-based solver, on a set of 383 LP instances derived from MIPLIB 2017, achieving a 6.3x reduction in the geometric mean of solve times with a target of 10⁻⁸ relative accuracy and 1 hour time limit.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e5ecb194-866c-432a-8d17-bb9a269dcc3b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:45.960Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9d8fdb23-8f21-47c3-b908-1deb8e71326b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e4b2c76d-f1ca-4e7d-8878-eb1553aa6339","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4HLXtkzThAgc9athUzUXM","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi CPLEX cuts external solver inject CP-SAT cut sharing portable\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Cuts – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4404952533905-Cuts\"},{\"title\":\"Cplex - Gurobi - UL HPC Tutorials\",\"url\":\"https://ulhpc-tutorials.readthedocs.io/en/latest/maths/Cplex-Gurobi/\"},{\"title\":\"Can I access the MIP cuts generated by Gurobi? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360040083172-Can-I-access-the-MIP-cuts-generated-by-Gurobi\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Separating specific cuts – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360048467412-Separating-specific-cuts\"},{\"title\":\"Gurobi cuts option – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360057766811-Gurobi-cuts-option\"},{\"title\":\"Comparative Studies of Quantum Annealing, Digital Annealing, and Classical Solvers for Reaction Network Pathway Analysis and mRNA Codon Selection\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09862v2\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CBC: A Practical Guide to the COIN-OR Solver | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cbc-a-practical-guide-to-the-coin-or-solver-fe5c1408d802\"},{\"title\":\"Controlling cut generation in the root node setting the CutPasses parameter – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360043314472-Controlling-cut-generation-in-the-root-node-setting-the-CutPasses-parameter\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found related to your query about Gurobi, CPLEX, cuts, external solvers, and CP-SAT:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Solver Comparison:**\nMathOpt is a modeling layer in OR-Tools that allows using CP-SAT as a backend solver, but also MIP solvers such as Gurobi or HiGHS.\n\n**Cut Generation in Solvers:**\nThe search results indicate that while solvers like Gurobi and CP-SAT generate cutting planes to improve their branch-and-bound algorithms, there are limitations:\n\n- It is not possible to access the cutting planes generated by Gurobi, as the cuts are generated in terms of the presolved model.\n- CP-SAT generates cuts mainly at \"level zero\" of its branch-and-bound process.\n\n**Performance Comparison:**\nOn standard and large protein datasets, Gurobi, CP-SAT, and Leap NL HQA solvers have the most reliable efficiency, with Gurobi showing the best scaling behavior.\n\nHowever, the search results don't specifically address topics like \"external solver injection,\" \"cut sharing between solvers,\" or portable formats for cut exchange between Gurobi, CPLEX, and CP-SAT. For more detailed information on those specific topics, you might want to consult the official documentation for each solver or research papers on solver integration techniques.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"19339c49-a1e9-4d7b-a118-9cdf5127a1b6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:46.004Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e4b2c76d-f1ca-4e7d-8878-eb1553aa6339","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c312de25-4203-4a7a-a5d3-e1e014d0d552","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L69G5TPzGGPar5oxPf1DLX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Combinatorial Benders Cuts Codato Fischetti placement scheduling\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/inm/oropre/v54y2006i4p756-766.html\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220244181_Combinatorial_Benders'_Cuts_for_Mixed-Integer_Linear_Programming\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming | Operations Research\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/abs/10.1287/opre.1060.0286\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Combinatorial Benders’ Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221316776_Combinatorial_Benders'_Cuts\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders’ Cuts | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-25960-2_14\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Combinatorial-Benders'-Cuts-for-Mixed-Integer-Codato-Fischetti/7ba61b0c68ee3b4557d888146f0f109593d96470\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders decomposition for single machine scheduling in additive manufacturing with two-dimensional packing constraints\",\"url\":\"https://ideas.repec.org/a/eee/ejores/v317y2024i3p890-905.html\"},{\"title\":\"A combinatorial Benders decomposition algorithm for ...\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10294466\"},{\"title\":\"Combinatorial Benders' Cuts for Mixed-Integer Linear Programming on JSTOR\",\"url\":\"https://www.jstor.org/stable/25147009\"},{\"title\":\"An accelerated Benders decomposition algorithm for integrated seaside operations planning with berthing preemption | Operational Research | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12351-025-00940-2\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Combinatorial Benders Cuts by Codato and Fischetti:\n\n## Overview\n\nGianni Codato and Matteo Fischetti developed Combinatorial Benders Cuts in 2006, published in Operations Research. Mixed-Integer Programs (MIPs) involving logical implications modelled through big-M coefficients are notoriously among the hardest to solve, and their approach proposes an automatic problem reformulation aimed at removing the model dependency on the big-M coefficients.\n\n## How It Works\n\nThe master solutions are sent to a slave linear program (LP), which validates them and possibly returns combinatorial inequalities to be added to the current master ILP. The inequalities are associated to minimal (or irreducible) infeasible subsystems of a certain linear system, and can be separated efficiently in case the master solution is integer.\n\nThe overall solution mechanism closely resembles the Benders' one, but the cuts produced are purely combinatorial and do not depend on the big-M values used in the MIP formulation. This produces an LP relaxation of the master problem which can be considerably tighter than the one associated with original MIP formulation.\n\n## Performance\n\nComputational results on two specific classes of hard-to-solve MIPs indicate that the new method produces a reformulation which can be solved some orders of magnitude faster than the original MIP model.\n\n## Applications to Scheduling and Placement\n\nThe search results show that Combinatorial Benders Cuts have been successfully applied to various scheduling problems, including assembly line balancing, additive manufacturing scheduling, and container terminal operations planning.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f0db3109-7896-496b-a80e-92bae1cf4d6b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:48.913Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c312de25-4203-4a7a-a5d3-e1e014d0d552","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4fc24998-213d-48f6-bcfb-c9305b1c82c5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XEwXWs6Q3kaaLpXmzA1dRY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"hybrid CP MIP Lagrangian relaxation lower bound CP-SAT branch and bound cooperation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT-Based Branch & Bound and Optimal Control of Hybrid Dynamical Systems | Springer Nature Link (formerly SpringerLink)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-24664-0_7\"},{\"title\":\"The Lagrangian Relaxation Method for Solving Integer Programming Problems | Management Science\",\"url\":\"https://pubsonline.informs.org/doi/10.1287/mnsc.27.1.1\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Programming Techniques for Mixed Integer ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.dei.unipd.it/~salvagni/pdf/phdthesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Lagrangian Relaxation Method for Solving Integer Programming Problems\",\"url\":\"https://my.ece.utah.edu/~kalla/phy_des/lagrange-relax-tutorial-fisher.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Branch and bound | Combinatorial Optimization Class Notes... | Fiveable\",\"url\":\"https://fiveable.me/combinatorial-optimization/unit-4/branch-bound/study-guide/6p8d0TSzwgBuWvhJ\"},{\"title\":\"Relaxations and Bounds: Applications to Knapsack Problems\",\"url\":\"https://sofdem.github.io/teach/oro/m2oro-ilp-demassey-notes-lec7-8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed-Integer Linear Programming, Constraint Programming and a Novel Dedicated Heuristic for Production Scheduling in a Packaging Plant\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3417/13/10/6003\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Lagrangian relaxation-based lower bound for the two-machine flow shop with synchronized period maintenance\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/323548350_Lagrangian_relaxation-based_lower_bound_for_the_two-machine_flow_shop_with_synchronized_period_maintenance\"},{\"title\":\"4.1 The Branch and Bound Approach Katta G. Murty Lecture slides\",\"url\":\"https://public.websites.umich.edu/~murty/614/614slides4.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found regarding hybrid CP/MIP approaches with Lagrangian relaxation and branch-and-bound cooperation:\n\n## Hybrid CP-MIP Integration\n\nA branch and bound procedure combines an MIP and a SAT solver to determine the optimal solution of optimization problems by exploring the search tree, solving at each node a linear relaxation and a satisfiability problem, until all integer variables are set to integer values in the optimal solution. When all integer variables are fixed, the procedure switches to the SAT solver which tries to extend the solution taking into account logical constraints, and if this is impossible, a \"no-good\" cut is generated and added to the linear relaxation.\n\n## Lagrangian Relaxation as Lower Bounds\n\nDualizing side constraints produces a Lagrangian problem that is easy to solve and provides a lower bound (for minimization problems) on the optimal value of the original problem, which can be used in place of a linear programming relaxation to provide bounds in a branch and bound algorithm.\n\n## CP-SAT and Branch-and-Cut\n\nCP-SAT employs Branch and Cut techniques, including linear relaxations and cutting planes, as part of its toolkit. The linear relaxation is used for detecting infeasibility, finding better bounds for the objective and variables, and making branching decisions using the linear relaxation's objective and the reduced costs.\n\n## Cooperation and Parallelization\n\nCP-SAT's different subsolvers operate largely independently but engage in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available, and the pragmatic strategy involves running various approaches in parallel with the hope that one will effectively address the problem at hand.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8ae3007f-0eda-48ef-9f71-79f6c2811e37","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:49.266Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4fc24998-213d-48f6-bcfb-c9305b1c82c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
