{"parentUuid":"77f480f5-61fe-42fd-abe0-2856adb61352","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NcGc2B5X3DhYGc6qUsQCbb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"linearization_level\" CP-SAT default 1 \"max_lp\" \"no_lp\" packing scheduling benchmark\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"Expected time to evaluate model (feasibility)\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/acul1GgXqf8\"},{\"title\":\"How to improve CP-SAT performance for large bin-packing problems? · Issue #1799 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1799\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the `linearization_level` parameter in CP-SAT:\n\n## Default Value\n\nThe default linearization_level is 1.\n\n## Linearization Levels\n\nCP-SAT supports different linearization levels with corresponding search strategies:\n\n- **default_lp** (linearization_level: 1): LCG-based search with default linearization of the model\n- **max_lp** (linearization_level: 2): Same as default_lp but with maximal linearization\n- **no_lp** (linearization_level: 0): Same as default_lp but without linearization\n\n## Practical Considerations\n\nFor packing and scheduling problems:\n\n- In packing problems, certain expensive propagation techniques can significantly speed up the search but can also drastically slow it down if misused\n- max_lp is probably a waste of resources if you know that your model has a terrible linear relaxation\n\nThe search results also show that CP-SAT runs multiple full problem subsolvers including default_lp, no_lp, and max_lp strategies, allowing the solver to use a portfolio approach that leverages different linearization levels in parallel.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"02b86b6b-4766-475d-9080-f9d09cd955a6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:24.843Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"77f480f5-61fe-42fd-abe0-2856adb61352","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1987a1aa-3c35-45bc-b9bf-5600d2f52d6e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017d7FT6wRzY4Gqru5w7MoLd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"HiGHS open source MIP cuts generator branch and cut Gomory clique\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"HiGHS - High-performance parallel linear optimization software\",\"url\":\"https://highs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS optimization solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HiGHS_optimization_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Why are Mixed integer programming solvers focused on finding cuts and not so much on search? - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/why-are-mixed-integer-programming-solvers-focused-on-finding-cuts-and-not-so-much-on-search/120945\"},{\"title\":\"Cuts\",\"url\":\"https://www-eio.upc.es/lceio/manuals/cplex-11/html/usrcplex/solveMIP14.html\"},{\"title\":\"HiGHS\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_HIGHS.html\"},{\"title\":\"About · HiGHS Documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ergo-code.github.io/HiGHS/dev/\"},{\"title\":\"CBC\",\"url\":\"https://www.gams.com/50/docs/S_CBC.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ERGO-Code/HiGHS: Linear optimization software · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction | Cbc\",\"url\":\"https://coin-or.github.io/Cbc/intro.html\"},{\"title\":\"Implementing cutting plane management and selection ...\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/3714.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about HiGHS and its capabilities regarding MIP cuts:\n\n## HiGHS Overview\n\nHiGHS is high performance serial and parallel software for solving large-scale sparse linear programming (LP), mixed-integer programming (MIP) and quadratic programming (QP) models, developed in C++11, with interfaces to C, C#, FORTRAN, Julia and Python. HiGHS is freely available under the MIT licence, and is downloaded from GitHub.\n\n## Branch-and-Cut for MIP\n\nHiGHS has a branch-and-cut solver for MIP problems. MIPs are solved by branch-and-cut, and the branch-and-cut MIP solver was written by Leona Gottwald.\n\n## Cuts in MIP Solving\n\nThe search results indicate that solvers like HiGHS add cuts at the root node (Gomory cut among other cuts) as part of their MIP solving strategy. However, the search results I found don't contain specific technical details about HiGHS's implementation of particular cut generators (Gomory cuts, clique cuts, etc.) or the detailed architecture of its MIP cuts generator module.\n\nFor more detailed technical information about HiGHS's specific cut generation algorithms and their implementation, you may want to consult the HiGHS GitHub repository (https://github.com/ERGO-Code/HiGHS) or contact the development team at hello@highs.dev.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"405b82e1-5af4-43b3-b670-16ddc50769df","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:27.522Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1987a1aa-3c35-45bc-b9bf-5600d2f52d6e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c99b215d-5211-4328-80dd-d0b8e9781983","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XdNfFEqwZip4MHPhR8h4Lp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"tight LP relaxation assignment problem placement x_ij integrality strong formulation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Linear programming relaxation - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_programming_relaxation\"},{\"title\":\"Relaxations and Bounds: Applications to Knapsack Problems\",\"url\":\"https://sofdem.github.io/teach/oro/m2oro-ilp-demassey-notes-lec7-8.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CS787: Advanced Algorithms Lecture 10: LP Relaxation and Rounding\",\"url\":\"https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~shuchi/courses/787-F09/scribe-notes/lec10.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction to Linear-Programming-Based LP- ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1673527\"},{\"title\":\"On the Strength of Linear Relaxations in Ordered Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.09166\"},{\"title\":\"CS 787: Advanced Algorithms LP-Based Approximations\",\"url\":\"https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~dieter/Courses/2004F-CS787/Scribes/lp-approx.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Linear Programming Relaxation - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/mathematics/linear-programming-relaxation\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 20: LP Relaxation and Approximation Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://yuanz.web.illinois.edu/teaching/B609fa16/L20.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: Lagrangean Relaxation for an Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2021/02/lagrangean-relaxation-for-assignment.html\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 3: Linear Programming Relaxations and Rounding 1\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.dartmouth.edu/~deepc/Courses/F10/Notes/lec3.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about tight LP relaxations for assignment problems with integrality and strong formulations:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Assignment Problem and Integrality:**\n\nSolving the LP relaxation of an assignment problem actually solves the problem itself, since every basic solution is integral. This is due to the total unimodularity of the matrix of constraint coefficients, which means that every square submatrix has a determinant of 1, –1, or 0.\n\n**Importance of Formulation Strength:**\n\nThe quality of the bound obtained by any LP relaxation depends on the strength of the formulation. Strong formulations and ideal formulations (where the extreme points of the polyhedron are integer) are usually hard to find—as hard as to solve the ILP—and may be of exponential size.\n\n**Tightness and Integrality Recovery:**\n\nThe efficiency of solving a MILP often depends critically on the tightness of its LP relaxation, that is, on how closely the relaxed feasible region approximates the convex hull of feasible integral solutions. In some special cases, as when the constraint matrix is totally unimodular, solving the LP relaxation is sufficient, as its solution coincides with the optimal integral one.\n\n**Strengthening Techniques:**\n\nA common strategy to improve relaxations is to strengthen a basic formulation by means of valid inequalities that tighten the feasible region toward the convex hull of integral solutions.\n\nFor the assignment problem specifically, the strong formulation properties are particularly favorable—the LP relaxation's integrality properties make it an ideal formulation for this problem class.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2633b6c8-37ec-467b-9b88-00a22e2967e1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:28.131Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c99b215d-5211-4328-80dd-d0b8e9781983","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b9b00e7b-11a0-4ee2-8e43-27f24c2c1841","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"acb01aa0ca95c3510","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMh9DZq7pML2GnDnPFst92","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"user cuts callback Gurobi extract lazy constraints reuse OR-Tools CP-SAT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"What is the difference between user cuts and lazy constraints? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360025804471-What-is-the-difference-between-user-cuts-and-lazy-constraints\"},{\"title\":\"Ignored lazy constraint leads to wrong solution – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360078071312-Ignored-lazy-constraint-leads-to-wrong-solution\"},{\"title\":\"3.5. Solving Technologies and Solver Backends — The MiniZinc Handbook 2.9.7\",\"url\":\"https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/stable/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"User Cuts and Lazy Constraints — AIMMS User's Guide\",\"url\":\"https://documentation.aimms.com/user-guide/aimms-ide/GUROBI/GUROBI_User_Cuts_and_Lazy_Constraints.html\"},{\"title\":\"How do I implement lazy constraints in Gurobi? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360013197972-How-do-I-implement-lazy-constraints-in-Gurobi\"},{\"title\":\"Obtain information on lazy constraint and user cut introduced – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4540069717905-Obtain-information-on-lazy-constraint-and-user-cut-introduced\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Constraints and Re-optimization – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360061662452-Lazy-Constraints-and-Re-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy constraints as general constraints? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/4410512476817-Lazy-constraints-as-general-constraints-\"},{\"title\":\"OR in an OB World: User Cuts versus Lazy Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://orinanobworld.blogspot.com/2012/08/user-cuts-versus-lazy-constraints.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Reference - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/parameters.html\"}]\n\nI found search results related to your query. Here's what the search returned:\n\nThe results primarily focus on **Gurobi's handling of user cuts and lazy constraints through callbacks**:\n\n**Key Distinctions:**\n- User cuts should never eliminate an integer solution that would otherwise be feasible, and the model plus all possible user cuts should have the same set of integer feasible solutions as the model without user cuts.\n- Lazy constraints are usually used to eliminate integer solutions that are otherwise feasible, and adding lazy constraints will affect the set of integer feasible solutions.\n\n**Callback Implementation:**\n- If you add lazy constraints via a callback, you must set the parameter LazyConstraints=1.\n- If constraints must be generated during the MIP search, you need to write a callback function and set the LazyConstraints parameter to 1.\n\n**Constraint Reuse and Extraction:**\nThe search results indicate that Gurobi \"forgets\" lazy constraints right after optimization, and you'll have to re-add the lazy constraints for every reoptimization.\n\nHowever, the search results did not return specific information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's approach to lazy constraints or user cuts, or about extracting and reusing constraints across different solve calls. If you need information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's constraint handling, that would require an additional search.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"85b29dd5-d7fe-46da-ba79-2d60106fb6c7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:29.522Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b9b00e7b-11a0-4ee2-8e43-27f24c2c1841","userT